E["npc:orgrim-doomhammer"] = {t="npc",n="Orgrim Doomhammer",z="arathi",s="Orgrim Doomhammer was the supreme Warchief of the Old Horde throughout the Second War, remembered as one of the greatest orc warriors in history. Though he died liberating the internment camps in the Arathi Highlands, his legacy endures in the capital of Orgrimmar and through Thrall, who inherited his mighty warhammer and black plate armor.",h="Orgrim Doomhammer was the supreme Warchief of the Old Horde throughout the Second War, remembered as one of...",sec={{t="Rise of the Warchief",b="Originally second-in-command to Blackhand of the Blackrock clan, Orgrim refused the demonic blood offered by Gul'dan, though he concealed his doubts beneath fierce loyalty. Near the close of the First War, disgusted by the Shadow Council's treachery and the murder of his childhood friend Durotan, Orgrim slew Blackhand in honorable combat. Assuming the mantle of Warchief, he ruthlessly purged Gul'dan's warlocks and led the Horde across the Eastern Kingdoms during the Second War. Though a devastating strategist who pushed human kingdoms to the brink of ruin, he was ultimately defeated and captured outside Blackrock Spire after the betrayal of Gul'dan split his forces.",sp=0},{t="Fall and Legacy",b="Escaping human captivity, Doomhammer lived in hiding until he met Thrall, Durotan's orphaned son. Reinvigorated by the young shaman's vision, Orgrim rallied what was left of the orcish clans to storm the internment camps and break their people free. During a fierce battle at an encampment in the Arathi Highlands, the Warchief was struck down from behind by a lance. As he lay dying, he bestowed his black plate armor, his ancestral weapon—the Doomhammer—and the title of Warchief upon Thrall. In his honor, the liberated outpost was renamed Hammerfall, and the newly founded capital in Durotar was christened Orgrimmar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Orgrim Doomhammer?",a="He was the Chieftain of the Blackrock clan and the Warchief who commanded the Horde during the Second War. After escaping human captivity years later, he fought alongside Thrall to liberate their imprisoned kin until his death in the Arathi Highlands.",al={"who is doomhammer","orgrim doomhammer background","who was warchief doomhammer"}},{q="How did Orgrim Doomhammer die?",a="Orgrim was slain during an assault on a human internment camp in the Arathi Highlands, struck from behind by a knight's lance. Thrall took up his mantle, and the site of that victory was named Hammerfall in memory of his sacrifice.",al={"orgrim doomhammer death","how did doomhammer die","who killed doomhammer"}},{q="Why is the Horde capital named Orgrimmar?",a="Thrall named the fortified city in Durotar to honor his mentor and predecessor. Orgrim saw the promise in Thrall and named him the new Warchief, ensuring the Horde would rebuild on honor rather than demonic corruption.",al={"why is it called orgrimmar","orgrimmar namesake","city named after orgrim"}},{q="Did Orgrim drink the demon blood?",a="No. Orgrim feigned humility, telling Blackhand and Gul'dan that a mere servant was not worthy to drink from the same cup as the Warchief. This clever excuse allowed him to retain his clarity and eventually destroy Gul'dan's Shadow Council from within.",al={"did doomhammer drink blood","was orgrim corrupted","orgrim demon blood"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Orcs revere Orgrim Doomhammer as the liberator who freed their people from lethargy and interned enslavement, choosing honor over demonic subjugation.",["faction:Alliance"]="To the Alliance, Doomhammer remains a grim symbol of the near-destruction of the Eastern Kingdoms during the Second War, having butchered countless champions before his defeat at Blackrock Spire."},kw={"blackhand","blackrock","doomhammer","hammerfall","orgrim","orgrimmar","thrall","warchief"},rel={"subzone:hammerfall","zone:orgrimmar","zone:arathi","topic:blackrock-clan","topic:old-horde","topic:second-war","topic:first-war","topic:horde"},src={"Orgrim Doomhammer"}}
E["npc:skuerto"] = {t="npc",n="Skuerto",z="arathi",s="Skuerto is a dwarven scout stationed at Refuge Pointe in the Arathi Highlands. Displaced from his home in Ironforge during the refugee crisis, he now aids the Alliance in the field, helping secure ancient magical relics on behalf of Archmage Malin.",h="Skuerto is a dwarven scout stationed at Refuge Pointe in the Arathi Highlands.",sec={{t="A Displaced Scout in the Highlands",b="Skuerto previously lived in Ironforge, but was displaced when city authorities made room to house thousands of gnome refugees escaping the radioactive fall of Gnomeregan. Relocating to the field, Skuerto took up work as a scout in the dangerous Arathi Highlands. Stationed alongside Apprentice Kryten at Refuge Pointe, he works under the direction of Archmage Malin to recover arcane reagents and potent magical artifacts that once belonged to Malin's old master, Archmage Trelane.",sp=0},{t="Pride and Peril",b="Despite the harsh conditions of the Highlands, Skuerto takes considerable pride in his wilderness scouting and reacts poorly to anyone questioning his competence. His work regularly brushes up against regional perils, from the hostile Syndicate and Boulderfist ogres to dangerous ancient entities tied to the land. Through his extensive travels and network of acquaintances, he maintains ties with diverse figures across the region, including Shakes O'Breen down at Faldir's Cove and Gerrig Bonegrip in the Ironforge forges.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Skuerto stationed in Arathi instead of Ironforge?",a="Skuerto used to live in Ironforge, but lost his living space when the city cleared quarters to take in gnome refugees fleeing the disaster at Gnomeregan. Left without a home in the mountain capital, he took employment out in the field as an Alliance scout.",al={"why is skuerto here","skuerto backstory","ironforge refugee"},it="why_here"},{q="What is Skuerto's mission at Refuge Pointe?",a="Archmage Malin sent Skuerto and Apprentice Kryten to the Arathi Highlands to collect arcane reagents and recover powerful magical artifacts once owned by Malin's former master, Archmage Trelane.",al={"skuerto purpose","what does skuerto do","skuerto malin"},it="purpose"},{q="Who are Skuerto's allies in the region?",a="Beyond working directly with Apprentice Kryten and the Alliance garrison at Refuge Pointe, Skuerto is friends with Shakes O'Breen hiding out at Faldir's Cove, as well as Gerrig Bonegrip in Ironforge.",al={"skuerto friends","shakes obreen friend"},it="allies"},{q="Does Skuerto hold a grudge against gnomes?",a="He harbors noticeable bitterness about losing his home in Ironforge to make room for displaced gnomes, though he remains dutifully in service to the Alliance cause out in Arathi.",al={"skuerto hates gnomes","skuerto gnomeregan"}},{q="Who is Skuerto?",a="Skuerto is an Ironforge dwarf scout stationed at Refuge Pointe in the Arathi Highlands. Proud of his reconnaissance skills and notably sensitive to criticism, he operates in the field alongside Apprentice Kryten on behalf of the Alliance.",al={"who is skuerto","skuerto identity","who is the dwarf skuerto"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Skuerto on?",a="Skuerto is firmly loyal to the Alliance and Ironforge. Operating out of the Alliance encampment at Refuge Pointe, he works in coordination with Dalaran mages and local Alliance forces against the threats looming over the Arathi Highlands.",al={"skuerto faction","is skuerto alliance","skuerto allegiances"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Skuerto want?",a="Skuerto wants to fulfill the mission given to him by Archmage Malin: securing magical reagents and reclaiming powerful lost artifacts that once belonged to Malin's late master, Archmage Trelane, all while defending his reputation as a capable scout.",al={"what does skuerto want","skuerto goals","skuerto motives"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Who is Skuerto tied to?",a="Beyond working under Archmage Malin and alongside Apprentice Kryten, Skuerto maintains personal connections across the Eastern Kingdoms. He counts the pirate Shakes O'Breen down at Faldir's Cove and Gerrig Bonegrip in Ironforge among his close acquaintances.",al={"skuerto ties","skuerto connections","who does skuerto know"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Skuerto exemplifies the grit of dwarves forced out of the Great Forge into wild frontiers, though his pride as a scout is easily bruised.",["race:Gnome"]="Gnomes may find a chilly reception from Skuerto, who was ousted from his Ironforge lodging when the capital opened its doors to refugees after Gnomeregan fell."},kw={"arathi highlands","archmage malin","ironforge","refuge pointe","scout","skuerto","trelane"},rel={"subzone:refuge-pointe","zone:arathi","npc:archmage-malin","subzone:faldir-s-cove","npc:gerrig-bonegrip","zone:ironforge","zone:gnomeregan","topic:alliance"},src={"Skuerto"}}
E["subzone:boulder-gor"] = {t="subzone",n="Boulder'gor",z="arathi",s="Boulder'gor is a rugged hill in the western Arathi Highlands, situated directly north of the ruined human kingdom of Stromgarde. It serves as an active encampment for the Boulderfist ogres and their unusual allies among the Witherbark forest trolls.",h="Boulder'gor is a rugged hill in the western Arathi Highlands, situated directly north of the ruined human...",sec={{t="A Den of Ogres and Trolls",b="Rising just north of the crumbling ramparts of Stromgarde Keep, Boulder'gor is a steep bluff claimed by the Boulderfist clan. Within its shadows sits the Boulderfist Outpost mound, making it a central bastion of ogre power across the highlands. Uniquely, the ogres here share their fires and fortifications with forest trolls of the Witherbark tribe, including shadowy spellcasters who lend their dark magic to the clan's brute force. This mutual cooperation poses an ongoing danger to any travelers passing along the central roads of Arathi.",sp=0},{t="Surrounding Territory",b="The slopes around Boulder'gor look down over the open highlands of western Arathi. Hemmed between the Syndicate-infiltrated ruins of Stromgarde and the wild elemental sites of the plains, Boulder'gor remains a heavily guarded and hostile stronghold of tribal solidarity against both Alliance and Horde wanderers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Boulder'gor?",a="Boulder'gor is an elevated hill and encampment north of Stromgarde Keep in the Arathi Highlands. It is heavily inhabited by Boulderfist ogres and Witherbark forest trolls.",al={"where is bouldergor","bouldergor info","what is this place"}},{q="Why are forest trolls living alongside ogres here?",a="The Witherbark trolls and Boulderfist ogres maintain a pragmatic alliance in Arathi. Both seek to maintain dominance over the highlands and fend off rival factions, pooling troll shadowcraft with brute ogre strength.",al={"why are trolls here","witherbark ogre alliance","trolls and ogres"}},{q="What major landmarks are near Boulder'gor?",a="Boulder'gor sits directly north of Stromgarde Keep, and the ogre mound of Boulderfist Outpost lies within the hill itself.",al={"nearby places","what is next to bouldergor","landmarks"}},{q="Is Boulder'gor friendly to the Horde or Alliance?",a="Neither. The Boulderfist ogres and Witherbark trolls of Boulder'gor are entirely hostile to both the Alliance and the Horde, aggressively defending their hill from outsiders.",al={"can i go there safely","is bouldergor hostile"}}},ang={["race:Troll"]="Darkspear trolls visiting the highlands will find no kinship here: the Witherbark forest trolls of Boulder'gor harbor deep ancient grudges against all outsiders, including other troll tribes.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance forces seeking to reclaim Stromgarde, Boulder'gor represents a serious threat lurking right on the fallen kingdom's northern doorstep."},kw={"arathi highlands","boulder'gor","boulderfist","bouldergor","ogres","stromgarde","witherbark"},rel={"subzone:boulderfist-outpost","subzone:stromgarde-keep","zone:arathi","topic:troll"},src={"Boulder'gor"}}
E["subzone:boulderfist-hall"] = {t="subzone",n="Boulderfist Hall",z="arathi",s="Boulderfist Hall is a heavily fortified ogre mound nestled in the southern hills of the Arathi Highlands, just north of Thandol Span. It serves as the local stronghold for the Boulderfist ogres, who exert their brute influence across the neighboring trade routes and valleys under the command of Kor'gresh Coldrage.",h="Boulderfist Hall is a heavily fortified ogre mound nestled in the southern hills of the Arathi Highlands...",sec={{t="A Bastion of Brute Strength",b="Carved into the rugged southern bluffs of the Arathi Highlands, Boulderfist Hall is the principal redoubt of the Boulderfist clan in the region. Sheltered within its earthen ramparts and deep caverns, ogre brutes and magi maintain a fortified settlement mere steps from Witherbark Village and the strategic bridge at Thandol Span. Deep within the mound lurks their regional chieftain, Kor'gresh Coldrage, alongside enforcers like Phalanax. From this stronghold, the ogres project violent control over the surrounding roads, making any peaceful transit between Arathi and the Wetlands perilous for travelers and supply caravans alike.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Boulderfist Hall?",a="It is a fortified ogre mound and cave complex in the southern Arathi Highlands, serving as the base of operations for the Boulderfist clan in this territory.",al={"what is this place","boulderfist mound","ogre cave arathi"}},{q="Who rules Boulderfist Hall?",a="The stronghold is led by the ogre chief Kor'gresh Coldrage, who directs his clan from the deep cavern inside the mound alongside champions like Phalanax.",al={"who leads boulderfist hall","ogre boss arathi","kor'gresh"}},{q="Why is this location strategically important?",a="Its proximity to Thandol Span allows the Boulderfist ogres to threaten the vital overland route connecting the Arathi Highlands to Khaz Modan, choking off traffic and skirmishing with neighboring trolls and travelers.",al={"why ogres here","thandol span danger"}},{q="Are the Boulderfist allied with the nearby Witherbark trolls?",a="No. The Boulderfist ogres and the forest trolls of Witherbark Village dwell in close proximity but remain independent and hostile factions competing for regional dominance in Arathi.",al={"ogres and trolls friends","witherbark alliance"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Positioned just above Thandol Span, the Boulderfist ogres pose a constant ambush hazard for Alliance couriers and reinforcements moving north from Ironforge into Arathi.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing the Arathi Highlands requires breaking the independent power of the ogres, clearing the southern ridge to safeguard Horde movement from Hammerfall."},kw={"arathi highlands","boulderfist","boulderfist hall","kor'gresh coldrage","ogre mound","phalanax","thandol span"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:thandol-span","subzone:witherbark-village"},src={"Boulderfist Hall"}}
E["subzone:boulderfist-outpost"] = {t="subzone",n="Boulderfist Outpost",z="arathi",s="Boulderfist Outpost is a fortified mound nestled deep within the ogre settlement of Boulder'gor in the Arathi Highlands. Serving as an interior den and holding area, it houses aggressive Boulderfist ogres alongside a few Witherbark trolls.",h="Boulderfist Outpost is a fortified mound nestled deep within the ogre settlement of Boulder'gor in the Arathi...",sec={{t="A Stronghold within the Mound",b="Carved into the earth and stone of western Arathi, Boulderfist Outpost functions as the heart of Boulder'gor. While brute enforcers dominate the settlement above, the outpost's interior concentrates the clan's core strength and provides a dark subterranean shelter. A handful of Witherbark troll witch doctors occasionally mingle among the ogres here, hinting at tenuous tribal cooperation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Boulderfist Outpost located?",a="Boulderfist Outpost is an interior mound found within the larger ogre settlement of Boulder'gor, situated in the western expanses of the Arathi Highlands.",al={"boulderfist outpost location","where is boulderfist outpost","boulderfist mound entrance"}},{q="Why are there trolls inside an ogre outpost?",a="Witherbark forest trolls dwell nearby in the Arathi Highlands and occasionally share ground with the Boulderfist ogres. A few Witherbark witch doctors can be found practicing their craft within the depths of the outpost alongside the ogres.",al={"why are witherbark here","trolls in boulderfist","witherbark trolls arathi"}},{q="Who is imprisoned in the outpost?",a="No named captives are known to be held in the outpost today. Its damp corridors belong to Boulderfist enforcers and a few Witherbark witch doctors, and anyone wandering inside should expect a fight rather than a rescue.",al={"boulderfist prisoners","who is trapped in boulderfist","captives in arathi ogres"}},{q="Who leads the ogres inside the outpost?",a="While the clan's brute enforcers patrol the interior, an exceptionally fierce ogre named Kovork is known to lurk within the mound as a notable threat.",al={"kovork","boulderfist boss arathi","boulderfist rare"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance scouts traveling Arathi should give the mound a wide berth, as the Boulderfist enforcers inside attack any intruder on sight.",["faction:Horde"]="The Boulderfist ogres make no distinction between factions, attacking Horde wanderers just as readily as their Alliance rivals."},kw={"arathi","boulder'gor","boulderfist","captives","kovork","ogre mound","prisoners","witherbark"},rel={"subzone:boulder-gor","zone:arathi","topic:troll"},src={"Boulderfist Outpost"}}
E["subzone:circle-of-east-binding"] = {t="subzone",n="Circle of East Binding",z="arathi",s="The Circle of East Binding is a mysterious ancient ritual site situated in the eastern reaches of the Arathi Highlands, just southwest of Hammerfall. Anchored by the Stone of East Binding, the site is violently contested and guarded by roaming water elementals known as cresting exiles.",h="The Circle of East Binding is a mysterious ancient ritual site situated in the eastern reaches of the Arathi...",sec={{t="The Eastern Ward",b="Positioned amidst the rugged highlands east of Stromgarde, the Circle of East Binding is one of several ancient sites of power scattered across the Arathi basin. At its focal point stands the Stone of East Binding, an enigmatic monument radiating potent elemental magic. Swirling water elementals known as cresting exiles roam the surrounding earth and fiercely defend the stone against any mortals who dare approach.",sp=0},{t="Elemental Imprisonment",b="The stones throughout Arathi are not mere natural anomalies; they function as ancient binding wards intended to suppress and imprison volatile elemental forces. The restless water spirits surrounding the eastern circle betray the strain on these wards, as the entities drawn to or trapped by the stone's magic lash out at travelers and adventurers navigating the nearby road to Hammerfall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Circle of East Binding located?",a="The Circle of East Binding is located in the eastern region of the Arathi Highlands, south of the main road and slightly southwest of the Horde encampment of Hammerfall.",al={"east binding location","where is circle of east binding","circle of east binding map"}},{q="What creatures are found here?",a="The circle is overrun by aggressive water elementals, the cresting exiles that relentlessly guard the Stone of East Binding.",al={"east binding mobs","what monsters are at east binding","cresting exiles"}},{q="Why are there water elementals in the highlands?",a="The stones scattered across Arathi serve as ancient elemental bindings. The presence of water elementals here points to the containment or attraction of aqueous elemental energy channeled through the eastern ward stone.",al={"why water elementals arathi","east binding elemental lore"}},{q="What is the purpose of the Stone of East Binding?",a="The Stone of East Binding is part of a coordinated network of binding stones throughout the Arathi Highlands designed to anchor, channel, and lock away volatile elemental entities.",al={"stone of east binding purpose","what does east binding stone do"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The binding stones in Arathi represent crude or ancient methods of elemental suppression, contrasting sharply with a shaman's pursuit of elemental balance and communion.",["faction:Horde"]="Lying just down the road from Hammerfall, the volatile water spirits around the circle pose an ongoing territorial nuisance for Horde patrols and supply lines."},kw={"arathi highlands","circle of east binding","cresting exile","cresting goliath","cresting guardian","elementals","hammerfall","stone of east binding"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:hammerfall"},src={"Circle of East Binding"}}
E["subzone:circle-of-inner-binding"] = {t="subzone",n="Circle of Inner Binding",z="arathi",s="The Circle of Inner Binding is an ancient ring of ritual stones situated in the southern hills of the Arathi Highlands, just east of Stromgarde Keep. Guarded by hostile earth elementals, it holds the Stone of Inner Binding, the most potent seal used to restrain the imprisoned elemental princess Myzrael deep beneath the earth.",h="The Circle of Inner Binding is an ancient ring of ritual stones situated in the southern hills of the Arathi...",sec={{t="The Core Seal",b="Perched upon a plateau south of the main road, the Circle of Inner Binding anchors the strongest of the ancient wards sealing Myzrael beneath Arathi. Towering slabs surround the central Stone of Inner Binding, which thrums with dense geo-magical power. Enormous rumbling earth elementals patrol the stones relentlessly, drawn to the site's resonance or bound as guardians. Despite these potent wards, cracks in this inner seal permit the trapped entity beneath the Highlands to reach out telepathically, whispering pleas for freedom to unsuspecting wanderers who handle shards of its stone.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Circle of Inner Binding?",a="The Circle houses the Stone of Inner Binding, which acts as the primary and strongest ward anchoring the subterranean prison of Myzrael. It works alongside other elemental circles scattered throughout the Arathi Highlands to keep the creature restrained beneath the surface.",al={"why is this circle here","what does the inner binding do","circle of inner binding lore"}},{q="What creatures guard this circle?",a="The circle is heavily guarded by powerful earth elementals, primarily Rumbling Exiles. These rocky behemoths aggressively attack anyone who approaches the ritual stones.",al={"what enemies are here","inner binding mobs","rumbling exile"}},{q="Who is whispering through the stone?",a="The voice reaching out through the binding shard belongs to Myzrael, an ancient and powerful elemental princess imprisoned deep beneath the earth. Her psychic reach has managed to pierce through this fractured seal to contact mortal minds.",al={"who talks to you here","myzrael voice","whispering stone"}},{q="Where is the Circle of Inner Binding located?",a="It is located in the southern portion of the Arathi Highlands, situated on the elevated ridgeline just east of the ruined stronghold of Stromgarde Keep.",al={"inner binding location","where is circle of inner binding","how to find inner binding"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The raw earthen energy surging through the Circle of Inner Binding indicates ancient, heavy elemental bonds, though the unnatural agitation of the local earth spirits warns of corruption beneath the soil.",["class:Mage"]="The geometric arrangement of the stones forms an intricate, long-lasting containment field capable of channeling and anchoring immense subterranean magical pressures."},kw={"arathi highlands","circle of inner binding","earth elementals","myzrael","rumbling exile","stone of inner binding","stromgarde keep"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:stromgarde-keep"},src={"Circle of Inner Binding"}}
E["subzone:circle-of-west-binding"] = {t="subzone",n="Circle of West Binding",z="arathi",s="The Circle of West Binding is one of several ancient ritual sites scattered across the Arathi Highlands, situated near Thoradin's Wall. Centered around the Stone of West Binding, this arcane ring is overrun by fiery elemental entities bound to the site.",h="The Circle of West Binding is one of several ancient ritual sites scattered across the Arathi Highlands...",sec={{t="The Western Keystone",b="Tucked against the rugged slopes near Thoradin's Wall, the Circle of West Binding forms part of a wider network of ritual sites dispersed throughout the Arathi Highlands. At its heart sits the Stone of West Binding, an ancient relic tied to elemental containment. The grounds are swarming with Burning Exiles—volatile fire elementals that relentlessly guard the perimeter, making any approach to the stone a perilous endeavor for travelers traversing the western plains.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Circle of West Binding?",a="It is an ancient ritual site in western Arathi Highlands, located near Thoradin's Wall. It holds the Stone of West Binding and is fiercely guarded by hostile fire elementals.",al={"circle of west binding","stone of west binding","west binding circle"}},{q="Why are there fire elementals here?",a="The Burning Exiles inhabit and guard the Stone of West Binding. They are elemental forces drawn or bound to the ancient magical foci constructed across the Arathi Highlands.",al={"burning exiles arathi","why fire elementals west binding","elementals circle of west binding"}},{q="Who is Ruul Onestone?",a="Ruul Onestone is a Boulderfist ogre mage who prowls the site, a rare and dangerous brute rather than a scholar of the binding stone.",al={"ruul onestone","ruul","dwarf at west binding"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The binding stones of Arathi offer arcane practitioners insight into how ancient mages and shamans anchored and subdued planar elemental entities.",["class:Shaman"]="The volatile presence of the Burning Exiles reveals the lingering elemental unrest tethered to these ancient Arathi keystones."},kw={"arathi highlands","burning exile","circle of west binding","elemental","ruul onestone","stone of west binding","thoradin's wall"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:thoradin-s-wall"},src={"Circle of West Binding"}}
E["subzone:crypt-stromgarde-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Crypt (Stromgarde Keep)",z="arathi",s="Deep within the ruins of Stromgarde Keep lies the royal crypt, situated past the sanctum chapel in the heart of the district held by the surviving Stromgarde defenders. It holds the tomb of the fallen King Thoras Trollbane and the ancestral treasures of his dynasty. Guarded closely by Prince Galen and faithful caretakers, the vault remains a sanctuary of royal honor amid a shattered kingdom.",h="Deep within the ruins of Stromgarde Keep lies the royal crypt, situated past the sanctum chapel in the heart...",sec={{t="The Tomb of Thoras Trollbane",b="Hidden beneath the Sanctum of Stromgarde Keep, this subterranean burial vault serves as the final resting place of King Thoras Trollbane, the warrior monarch who led Stromgarde through the Second War. Despite the devastation engulfing the city—split among Syndicate rogues and Boulderfist ogres—the remaining Stromgarde militia fiercely maintains their grip on this quarter. Prince Galen Trollbane personally watches over the crypts alongside dedicated royal caretakers, ensuring his father's body and legacy remain undisturbed by the scavengers and enemies outside.",sp=0},{t="The Vault of Trol'kalar",b="Beyond housing the royal dead, the crypt safeguards prized artifacts belonging to the Trollbane lineage. Chief among these relics is Trol'kalar, the ancient runed greatsword forged centuries ago to slay trolls. Entrusted to the sworn protection of caretakers such as Alaric, Nevlin, and Weston, the chamber and its treasures are secured with powerful safeguards. Galen and his loyalists guard the tomb relentlessly, well aware that rival factions and hostile trolls across Arathi would covet the blade's ancient power.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is buried in the crypt?",a="King Thoras Trollbane, the late ruler of Stromgarde, is interred here. His son, Prince Galen Trollbane, keeps watch over the tomb amidst the ruined city.",al={"who is buried here","whose tomb is this","crypt tomb"}},{q="What is Trol'kalar?",a="Trol'kalar is an ancient heirloom blade belonging to the Trollbane family. Its name translates from the ancient tongue to mean 'troll slayer,' and it was originally forged to fight the forest trolls of the Arathi basin.",al={"trolkalar sword","trollbane sword","what is trolkalar"}},{q="Who guards the crypt?",a="The crypt is defended by Prince Galen Trollbane and the Stromgarde royal caretakers, including Alaric, Nevlin, and Weston. They protect the burial chamber from encroaching Syndicate thieves and Boulderfist ogres.",al={"crypt guards","who defends the crypt","caretakers"}},{q="Where is the crypt located?",a="It is located within Stromgarde Keep in the Arathi Highlands, found deep inside the Sanctum district behind the keep's chapel, in the sector still held by Stromgarde loyalists.",al={"crypt location","how to find the crypt","where is stromgarde crypt"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="For humans of the Alliance, the tomb represents the tragic decline of Stromgarde, one of the seven great kingdoms, and the hallowed grave of one of the Alliance's fiercest wartime leaders.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stromgarde's royal crypt stands as one of the last bastions of Alliance heritage in Arathi, guarded tenaciously against bandits, ogres, and the Horde."},kw={"arathi","crypt","galen","sanctum","stromgarde","thoras","trol'kalar","trollbane"},rel={"subzone:sanctum-stromgarde-keep","subzone:stromgarde-keep","zone:arathi","topic:troll"},src={"Crypt (Stromgarde Keep)"}}
E["subzone:dabyrie-s-farmstead"] = {t="subzone",n="Dabyrie's Farmstead",z="arathi",s="Dabyrie's Farmstead is an Alliance-aligned rural settlement situated in northern Arathi Highlands. In a realm shattered by the Third War and overrun by Syndicate outlaws and Witherbark trolls, this estate remains a stubborn bastion of Stromgarde citizens led by Kenata Dabyrie.",h="Dabyrie's Farmstead is an Alliance-aligned rural settlement situated in northern Arathi Highlands.",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Highlands",b="Perched in the northern fields of the Arathi Highlands, Dabyrie's Farmstead is one of the very few functioning human homesteads remaining in the fractured kingdom of Stromgarde. Owned by Kenata Dabyrie and worked alongside her sons, Fardel and Marcel, the grounds are fiercely defended by a local family militia. Surrounded by aggressive wildlife, opportunistic bandits, and the nearby Forsaken presence in the north, the farm stands as a symbol of human endurance in a ruined land.",sp=0},{t="Bitter Feuds",b="Survival in Arathi rarely comes without bitter enmity. The estate has drawn the intense ire of the Forsaken, particularly Genavie Callow, a former noblewoman who lost her lands and kin during the Third War. Callow accuses the surviving Dabyrie clan of looting her family's precious heirlooms in the chaos of the plague, transforming the modest farmstead into a target of vengeful Horde mercenaries seeking to settle old northern grudges.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who lives at Dabyrie's Farmstead?",a="The farm is the home of Kenata Dabyrie and her sons, Fardel and Marcel. They are human citizens of Stromgarde loyal to the Alliance, protected by a sworn local militia.",al={"who owns dabyrie farm","dabyrie family","kenata dabyrie"}},{q="Why is the Horde targeting this farm?",a="A Forsaken woman named Genavie Callow harbors a grudge against the Dabyries. She claims they plundered her family's estate and made off with her surviving heirlooms while her own relatives perished in the Third War.",al={"why kill dabyrie","genavie callow quest","horde dabyrie quest"}},{q="Is Dabyrie's Farmstead part of Stromgarde?",a="Yes. The Dabyries consider themselves subjects of the kingdom of Stromgarde and allies of the broader Alliance, holding fast despite the collapse of their central capital to the south.",al={"is dabyrie alliance","stromgarde farm"}},{q="What threats surround the farmstead?",a="The farm sits dangerously close to hostile highlands predators, roaming Syndicate cutthroats, and Forsaken forces pressing down across the borders from the north.",al={"threats to dabyrie","danger near dabyrie farm"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers, the farmstead is a rare and comforting reminder that Stromgarde's people still survive and fight for their land amidst encroaching enemies.",["race:Undead"]="To the Forsaken, the prosperous homestead is an irritating spectacle of living humans hoarding goods looted from families who perished during the Third War."},kw={"arathi","callow","dabyrie","fardel","farmstead","kenata","marcel","stromgarde"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:stromgarde-keep","topic:forsaken","topic:alliance","topic:third-war","topic:syndicate"},src={"Dabyrie's Farmstead"}}
E["subzone:drowned-reef"] = {t="subzone",n="Drowned Reef",z="arathi",s="The Drowned Reef is a treacherous stretch of coastal waters off the southern cliffs of the Arathi Highlands. Beneath the waves lie ancient sunken ruins, claimed by hostile Daggerspine naga who manipulate the tides to dash passing vessels against the jagged shoals.",h="The Drowned Reef is a treacherous stretch of coastal waters off the southern cliffs of the Arathi Highlands.",sec={{t="A Graveyard of Ships",b="Just outside the hidden entrance to Faldir's Cove, the Drowned Reef forms a watery graveyard for careless navigators. Shattered hulks, such as the Maiden's Folly and the Spirit of Silverpine, lie submerged beneath the waves. While treacherous rocks pose a natural hazard, the real peril stems from the resident Daggerspine naga led by Prince Nazjak. These serpentine creatures command the local tides, actively dragging vulnerable ships onto the stones to scavenge their cargo and drown their crews.",sp=0},{t="The Sunken City",b="Those brave or foolish enough to dive into the deep water will discover the submerged architecture of an ancient elven city. Calcified elven gems remain among its drowned ruins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Drowned Reef?",a="The Drowned Reef is a hazardous marine zone along the southern coast of the Arathi Highlands, situated just offshore from Faldir's Cove. It is known for its shallow, ship-breaking shoals and ancient ruins lurking beneath the sea.",al={"drowned reef","where is drowned reef","arathi reef"}},{q="Why are there so many sunken ships here?",a="Ships attempting to reach Faldir's Cove or navigate the Arathi coast frequently run aground here. The Daggerspine naga who infest the reef possess the power to control the local tides, deliberately steering vessels into the jagged rocks to wreck them.",al={"why are ships sinking","sunken ships arathi","maidens folly"}},{q="Who controls the Drowned Reef?",a="The reef is inhabited by the Daggerspine tribe of naga, who dwell within the flooded ruins. Their local forces are directed by Prince Nazjak, who commands them to prey upon stranded sailors and protect their submerged territory.",al={"who leads the naga here","prince nazjak","daggerspine naga arathi"}},{q="What are the ruins submerged beneath the reef?",a="The reef contains the ruins of an ancient elven city, with calcified elven gems among its submerged remains.",al={"underwater ruins arathi","elven ruins drowned reef"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="The flooded halls beneath the reef and the calcified gems resting in the seabed are somber reminders of the Kaldorei empire that shattered into the sea ten thousand years ago during the Great Sundering."},kw={"arathi highlands","daggerspine","drowned reef","faldir's cove","maiden's folly","naga","prince nazjak","spirit of silverpine","sunken ruins"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:faldir-s-cove","topic:naga"},src={"Drowned Reef"}}
E["subzone:drywhisker-gorge"] = {t="subzone",n="Drywhisker Gorge",z="arathi",s="Drywhisker Gorge is a rugged cleft in the eastern mountains of the Arathi Highlands, situated northeast of the Horde outpost of Hammerfall. The gorge and its inner cavern are held by a hostile clan of kobolds, who fiercely guard rich mineral deposits and ancient elemental relics buried deep underground.",h="Drywhisker Gorge is a rugged cleft in the eastern mountains of the Arathi Highlands, situated northeast of...",sec={{t="A Warren in the Eastern Crags",b="Tucked away in the mountainous folds east of Hammerfall, Drywhisker Gorge serves as the primary redoubt of the Drywhisker clan of kobolds. While kobolds are often dismissed as simple mine pests, the Drywhiskers in Arathi are heavily entrenched. They guard their subterranean passages with fierce territorial tenacity, working veins of rare Lesser Bloodstone Ore and defending the deep recesses of the earth. Their proximity makes them a persistent nuisance to the nearby orcs of Hammerfall.",sp=0},{t="Secrets of the Deep Cavern",b="Venture far enough past the torchlit barricades and winding tunnels, and the cavern reveals a darker secret than ordinary pickaxes and candles. Allied with the towering stone giants of the highlands, the Drywhisker kobolds attend to motes of ancient earth magic. Deep in the heart of the cave lies a mysterious stone shard that houses a trapped fragment of the essence of Princess Myzrael, an ancient earth entity bound below the surface.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who lives in Drywhisker Gorge?",a="The gorge and its cavern network are inhabited by the Drywhisker clan of kobolds. They aggressively defend their territory from outsiders, guarding both their mining operations and ancient relics hidden within.",al={"drywhisker gorge inhabitants","what is in drywhisker gorge","who controls drywhisker gorge"}},{q="Where is Drywhisker Gorge located?",a="The gorge cuts through the craggy eastern mountains of the Arathi Highlands, directly northeast of the Horde settlement of Hammerfall. A rugged path leads up through the hills east of the outpost to reach the cavern entrance.",al={"how to get to drywhisker gorge","drywhisker gorge location","where is the cave in arathi"}},{q="What makes the cave inside significant?",a="Beyond containing rare deposits of Lesser Bloodstone Ore, the cave shelters an ancient stone shard. This relic contains a fragment of the imprisoned essence of Princess Myzrael, a powerful subterranean entity.",al={"what is in the cave","drywhisker cave secrets","myzrael shard"}},{q="Why are the kobolds allied with mountain giants?",a="The Drywhisker clan shares a connection with the local stone giants, serving and guarding the earth relics and elemental motes tied to the bindings of Princess Myzrael deep beneath Arathi.",al={"kobolds and giants","why are drywhiskers with giants"}}},ang={["profession:Mining"]="Miners prize the Drywhisker cavern as the only known source of Lesser Bloodstone Ore, a dense, crimson-veined mineral embedded deep within the kobold-infested rock.",["faction:Horde"]="Resting right over the mountain ridge from Hammerfall, the hostile Drywhisker kobolds represent an unpredictable threat lingering on the outpost's eastern flank."},kw={"arathi highlands","drywhisker","drywhisker gorge","hammerfall","kobold","lesser bloodstone ore","princess myzrael","stone shard"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:hammerfall","topic:kobold"},src={"Drywhisker Gorge"}}
E["subzone:faldir-s-cove"] = {t="subzone",n="Faldir's Cove",z="arathi",s="Faldir's Cove is a secluded natural harbor nestled along the southern coastline of the Arathi Highlands. Steeped in human history, it is traditionally remembered as the departure point from which early settlers sailed south to found Stormwind. Today, it serves as an emergency shelter for stranded Blackwater Raiders whose fleet ran afoul of local hazards.",h="Faldir's Cove is a secluded natural harbor nestled along the southern coastline of the Arathi Highlands.",sec={{t="A Gateway South and a Pirate Haven",b="Tucked away behind the rugged bluffs south of Stromgarde Keep, Faldir's Cove is linked to the mainland by a concealed cave tunnel. The cove honors the memory of Faldir, the ancient Arathor explorer whose expedition set sail from these very shores to cross the Great Sea and establish the southern kingdom of Stormwind. In the present day, however, its quiet waters house a very different crowd: an expedition of Blackwater Raiders from Booty Bay, led by Captains Steelgut and O'Breen, who sailed north pursuing ancient elven treasures only to end up trapped in the bay.",sp=0},{t="The Wreck of the Blackwater Fleet",b="The Blackwater venture turned catastrophic upon reaching the Arathi coast. Strange and unnatural tides conjured by the territorial naga dwelling on the offshore Drowned Reef shattered two of their three vessels. Only the Harbinger survived intact, limping into Faldir's Cove. With the naga prowling the waters and their navigation charts resting beneath the waves, the surviving pirates and their gnomish researchers find themselves marooned, reliant on neutral travelers to battle the aquatic horrors and recover sunken salvage.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Faldir?",a="Faldir was an ancient pioneer from the early human empire of Arathor. He and his followers embarked from this coastal haven to sail across the seas, journeying south to establish the settlements that eventually became the kingdom of Stormwind.",al={"faldir lore","who is faldir","faldir founder"}},{q="How do you reach Faldir's Cove?",a="The cove is reached by finding a hidden tunnel passage located just southeast of the outer southern walls of Stromgarde Keep. Walking through this subterranean tunnel brings travelers directly out onto the secluded shore.",al={"how to get to faldir's cove","faldir cove entrance","cave to faldirs cove"}},{q="Why are the Blackwater Raiders here?",a="Captain Steelgut and Captain O'Breen led an expedition north from Booty Bay in search of sunken elven treasures. Along with gnomish inventors who designed gem-detecting apparatuses, they aimed to salvage precious relics calcified within the offshore reefs.",al={"why are pirates here","blackwater raiders arathi","what are the pirates doing"}},{q="What happened to their ships?",a="Two of the expedition's three vessels were destroyed by unnatural tides stirred up by hostile naga inhabiting the Drowned Reef. Only the flagship Harbinger safely made port in the cove, leaving the crew stranded without their sunken charts.",al={"why are ships wrecked","sunken ships arathi","who sank the ships"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="Standing upon these shores connects humans to their early heritage, marking the historic launching point where the ancestors of Stormwind parted from the ancient empire of Arathor.",["race:Gnome"]="The camp features Doctor Draxlegauge and Professor Phizzlethorpe, who have deployed ingenious engineering contraptions to analyze and extract elven gems from calcified coastal reefs."},kw={"blackwater raiders","captain o'breen","captain steelgut","draxlegauge","drowned reef","faldir","faldir's cove","harbinger","phizzlethorpe"},rel={"subzone:drowned-reef","zone:arathi","subzone:stromgarde-keep","subzone:booty-bay","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:naga"},src={"Faldir's Cove"}}
E["subzone:go-shek-farm"] = {t="subzone",n="Go'Shek Farm",z="arathi",s="Go'Shek Farm is an agricultural outpost in the eastern Arathi Highlands, occupied by the Horde and guarded by orcs from Hammerfall. Behind its mundane rural facade, Forsaken apothecaries conduct secretive alchemical experiments far from prying eyes.",h="Go'Shek Farm is an agricultural outpost in the eastern Arathi Highlands, occupied by the Horde and guarded by...",sec={{t="A Horde Outpost in the East",b="Once a human farmstead held by Second War veterans, Go'Shek Farm fell into Horde hands following the chaos of the Third War. Positioned south of Hammerfall and just north of the hostile Witherbark troll territory, the farmstead nominally serves as a vital supply and staging hub for the orcish settlement. Hammerfall Grunts patrol the fields and stables, securing food and livestock to sustain the Horde's embattled foothold in the Arathi Highlands.",sp=0},{t="The Apothecary's Workshop",b="Beneath the routine work of tilling soil and tending beasts lies a darker purpose. The Royal Apothecary Society has established a quiet presence at the farmstead, led by figures such as Apothecary Jorell. Couriers slip between Go'Shek Farm and Tarren Mill, ferrying notes, reagents, and research into early variants of the Forsaken's new plague. The Alliance has taken notice, dispatching scouts to intercept these messengers and uncover the nature of the poison brewing in the Arathi soil.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is the Horde occupying Go'Shek Farm?",a="The farmstead provides essential agricultural supplies and livestock for the nearby orc stronghold of Hammerfall. Additionally, it gives the Forsaken a discreet, guarded staging ground to conduct sensitive chemical and alchemical research.",al={"who owns goshek farm","why are orcs at goshek farm","goshek farm horde"}},{q="Who used to own this farm?",a="It was originally a human farmstead, occupied by human veterans of the Second War such as Primwell Skye, before the devastation of the Third War allowed the Horde to claim the land.",al={"goshek farm history","human farm arathi","primwell skye"}},{q="What kind of experiments are happening here?",a="Forsaken apothecaries, including Apothecary Jorell, use the remote farm to test and refine early formulas for a new plague. They correspond and trade research materials with fellow apothecaries in Tarren Mill.",al={"apothecary jorell","plague experiments arathi","forsaken research goshek"}},{q="Why are there Alliance agents watching the farm?",a="Alliance scouts Quae and Kinelory were dispatched to monitor suspicious courier movements between the farmstead and Tarren Mill. They seek to intercept Forsaken dispatches and determine what biological threats the Undercity is concocting.",al={"quae kinelory","alliance scouting goshek","hints of a new plague"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Go'Shek Farm represents a dual threat: an agricultural artery feeding the garrison at Hammerfall, and a covert laboratory developing toxic Forsaken contagions.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing the farm is critical to keeping Hammerfall provisioned, while also maintaining a heavily fortified perimeter against the encroaching Witherbark trolls."},kw={"apothecary jorell","arathi","go'shek farm","goshek","hammerfall","kinelory","quae","swee","witherbark"},rel={"subzone:hammerfall","zone:arathi","subzone:tarren-mill","quest:367","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","subzone:witherbark-village","topic:alliance"},src={"Go'Shek Farm"}}
E["subzone:hammerfall"] = {t="subzone",n="Hammerfall",z="arathi",s="Hammerfall is the Horde's primary fortified outpost in the Arathi Highlands, built upon the ruins of a notorious Alliance internment camp. It honors the legendary former Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer, who fell nearby while fighting to liberate his captive people. Today, orcs and Forsaken garrison the settlement against hostile Boulderfist ogres, Witherbark trolls, and the League of Arathor.",h="Hammerfall is the Horde's primary fortified outpost in the Arathi Highlands, built upon the ruins of a...",sec={{t="A Legacy of Liberation",b="Following the Second War, the human Alliance built vast internment camps across Lordaeron to contain the defeated orcs. The compound that once stood here was among the largest. Years later, Thrall and Orgrim Doomhammer assaulted the camp to liberate the lethargic captives. During the chaos of their retreat, a charging Alliance knight drove a lance through Doomhammer's backplate, mortally wounding the legendary Warchief. Following the Third War, the new Horde reclaimed the ruined ground and established an outpost here, naming it Hammerfall in memory of their fallen leader.",sp=0},{t="A Foothold in the Highlands",b="Today, Hammerfall serves as the Horde's lifeline in Arathi. Positioned against hostile surroundings, the garrison contends with aggressive Boulderfist ogres from Boulder'gor and Boulderfist Hall, as well as the native Witherbark trolls. Furthermore, Forsaken Defilers have made the outpost their staging ground to claim the contested resources of the Arathi Basin against the Alliance's League of Arathor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this base called Hammerfall?",a="It is named in honor of former Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer, who was mortally wounded on this ground by an Alliance knight's lance during the liberation of the orc internment camp.",al={"why hammerfall","hammerfall name origin","who died at hammerfall"}},{q="What was Hammerfall before the Horde rebuilt it?",a="It was one of the largest Alliance of Lordaeron internment camps, constructed after the Second War to imprison captive orcs.",al={"hammerfall history","what was hammerfall before","internment camp arathi"}},{q="Who leads the defense of Hammerfall right now?",a="Horde figures like Drum Fel and Tallow coordinate the outpost's defense, directing warriors against the encroaching Boulderfist ogres and Witherbark forest trolls.",al={"hammerfall leaders","who is in charge of hammerfall","tallow drum fel"}},{q="Why are the Forsaken stationed here?",a="The Forsaken Defilers operate out of Hammerfall to secure vital supplies from the Arathi Basin and counter the Alliance's League of Arathor.",al={"forsaken hammerfall","why are undead in hammerfall","defilers arathi"}}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Hammerfall is hallowed ground for orcs, marking the place where Orgrim Doomhammer gave his life to free captive clanmates and pass the mantle of Warchief to Thrall.",["faction:Horde"]="Surrounded by hostile ogres, forest trolls, and remnants of the Alliance, Hammerfall is the Horde's sole fortress ensuring control over the central Arathi Highlands."},kw={"arathi highlands","boulderfist","defilers","hammerfall","internment camp","orgrim doomhammer","thrall","witherbark"},rel={"npc:orgrim-doomhammer","zone:arathi","npc:thrall","npc:drum-fel","npc:tallow","subzone:boulder-gor","subzone:boulderfist-hall","topic:second-war"},src={"Hammerfall"}}
E["subzone:northfold-manor"] = {t="subzone",n="Northfold Manor",z="arathi",s="Northfold Manor is a dilapidated agricultural estate situated on the northwestern fringes of the Arathi Highlands. Once a prosperous human homestead before the collapse of Stromgarde, the grounds are now occupied by criminal operatives of the Syndicate engaging in unsettling, dark practices.",h="Northfold Manor is a dilapidated agricultural estate situated on the northwestern fringes of the Arathi...",sec={{t="A Den of Brigands",b="Perched on the rolling highlands near the Thoradin's Wall passage, Northfold Manor once supported the kingdom of Stromgarde. In the chaos following the realm's fracturing, displaced Alteraci nobility and outlaws of the Syndicate claimed the manor house, barn, and fields as an operational base. Instead of tending crops, Syndicate mercenaries, highwaymen, and pathstalkers use the farmstead to stage ambushes along the roads and coordinate their presence across Arathi.",sp=0},{t="Demonic Undertones",b="Behind the everyday thievery and armed posturing, Northfold Manor harbors more sinister pursuits. Lingering traces of demonic summoning cling to the farmstead, felt keenly by sensitive spellcasters and shamans in the region. Discarded bloodstone amulets—potent talismans used to fuel dark invocations—litter the grounds, indicating that the Syndicate rogues here are entangling themselves with demonic magic far beyond simple banditry.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who controls Northfold Manor?",a="The estate has fallen into the hands of the Syndicate, an organization of dispossessed Alteraci nobles, bandits, and rogue mercenaries who now use the property as an armed encampment.",al={"who lives here","who owns northfold","syndicate farm"}},{q="What dark magic is being practiced here?",a="Visitors sensitive to magical energies detect residual traces of demonic summoning. The Syndicate forces stationed at the manor possess bloodstone amulets, used to channel and assist in dangerous demonic rituals.",al={"demons at northfold","bloodstone","what are they summoning"}},{q="Why does the Horde care about this farm?",a="The troll shaman Tor'gan at Hammerfall sensed an unnatural disturbance brewing across the highlands. Investigating the source led him directly to Northfold Manor, prompting the Horde to investigate the Syndicate's occult activities.",al={"horde interest northfold","why tor'gan cares"}},{q="Who is Singer?",a="Singer is an elusive Syndicate figure occasionally spotted lurking inside the main house of Northfold Manor among the other brigands.",al={"singer","singer rare","who is singer"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The shamans of Hammerfall closely watch Northfold Manor, dispatching warriors to seize the bloodstone talismans the Syndicate uses to dabble in demonic summoning.",["class:Shaman"]="The demonic residue lingering over Northfold Manor disrupts the natural elements, causing spiritual unease and fiery rage in attuned shamans who draw near."},kw={"arathi highlands","bloodstone","northfold manor","singer","stromgarde","syndicate","tor'gan"},rel={"topic:syndicate","zone:arathi","topic:horde","quest:255","topic:troll"},src={"Northfold Manor"}}
E["subzone:refuge-pointe"] = {t="subzone",n="Refuge Pointe",z="arathi",s="Refuge Pointe is the primary redoubt for the Alliance and the surviving remnants of Stromgarde within the Arathi Highlands. Perched centrally along the highlands' trade road, it serves as a staging ground to reclaim the shattered capital of Stromgarde Keep and hold back rival forces across the region.",h="Refuge Pointe is the primary redoubt for the Alliance and the surviving remnants of Stromgarde within the...",sec={{t="A Bastion for Stromgarde's Remnants",b="Following the devastation of the Third War and the catastrophic fall of Stromgarde Keep, the bulk of Stromgarde's surviving populace fled south toward friendlier lands. Those who remained formed a resolute vanguard, digging in at Refuge Pointe under Captain Nials. Composed of battle-hardened Stromgarde soldiers, League of Arathor forces, and supporting Alliance specialists, the encampment represents the kingdom's last organized stand in its ancestral homeland.",sp=0},{t="Stretched to the Limit",b="Refuge Pointe is constantly on the brink of being overwhelmed. Hemmed in by the Forsaken and the Horde based out of Hammerfall, Witherbark trolls, Syndicate rogues, and Boulderfist ogres, the garrison has zero reserves to spare. When dwarven commanders at the battered Thandol Span desperately requested reinforcements to fight off the Dark Iron clan, Captain Nials had to refuse. Every sword, shield, and scrap of supply stationed at Refuge Pointe must remain dedicated to defending the highlands and preparing a counteroffensive to retake Stromgarde Keep.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Alliance presence here so small?",a="The kingdom of Stromgarde fell into ruin following the Third War, forcing most surviving civilians to evacuate south. The troops at Refuge Pointe are an embattled remnant of the Stromic army, bolstered by an expeditionary Alliance force. With supplies stretched thin and enemies on every front, they can barely hold their fortified camp.",al={"why is refuge pointe small","why so few soldiers","alliance numbers arathi"}},{q="Why won't Refuge Pointe send soldiers to help at the Thandol Span?",a="When dwarven messengers arrived asking for troops to defend Dun Modr and the Thandol Span from Dark Iron assaults, Captain Nials had to decline. With Stromgarde Keep overrun and hostile forces surrounding them, duty and survival demand that every soldier stay committed to holding the highlands and retaking their fallen capital.",al={"why no help dun modr","captain nials thandol span","plea to the alliance quest"}},{q="Who commands the camp?",a="Captain Nials commands the garrison at Refuge Pointe. She directs Stromgarde's military operations across the highlands, coordinating scouting efforts, skirmishes against the Syndicate and ogres, and defensive patrols along the main road.",al={"refuge pointe leader","who is in charge here","captain nials"}},{q="What is the League of Arathor?",a="The League of Arathor is an Alliance coalition committed to reclaiming the Arathi Highlands and securing vital resources in the neighboring Arathi Basin. Operating alongside Stromgarde's remnant forces at Refuge Pointe, they fight to deny the Forsaken-led Defilers control of the fertile valley.",al={"league of arathor","who are league of arathor","arathi basin alliance"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="Refuge Pointe serves as your sole military sanctuary and flight hub in the Arathi Highlands, offering critical relief in a dangerous territory contested by ogres, the Syndicate, and the Horde.",["race:Human"]="For humans, Refuge Pointe is a poignant reminder of Stromgarde's former glory as humanity's martial heartland, where stalwart defenders refuse to abandon their homeland despite overwhelming odds."},kw={"arathi highlands","arathor","captain nials","league of arathor","refuge pointe","stromgarde","thandol span"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:stromgarde-keep","quest:634","subzone:thandol-span","topic:alliance","npc:longbraid-the-grim","npc:skuerto","topic:third-war"},src={"Refuge Pointe"}}
E["subzone:sanctum-stromgarde-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Sanctum (Stromgarde Keep)",z="arathi",s="The Sanctum is a sacred redoubt tucked behind the chapel within Stromgarde Keep. Sheltered within the crumbling fortress, it guards the entrance to the ancestral Trollbane family crypt and stands as one of the few remaining bastions of the Holy Light amidst Arathi's ruin.",h="The Sanctum is a sacred redoubt tucked behind the chapel within Stromgarde Keep.",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Ruins",b="While much of Stromgarde Keep has fallen to Syndicate infiltrators and the Boulderfist ogres, the Sanctum and its adjacent chapel have remained under the fierce protection of the surviving Stromgarde defenders. Located behind the house of worship, the Sanctum borders the citadel's graveyard and marks the threshold to the royal crypt where the kings of Stromgarde rest. For the battered loyalists rallying around Prince Galen Trollbane, holding this hallowed ground represents more than a tactical foothold; it is a desperate fight to keep their kingdom's ancestral heritage and faith from being trampled by invaders.",sp=0},{t="Threshold of the Kings",b="Beneath the stone flags of the Sanctum lies the passage into the royal tomb. The ground here is consecrated, intended as a place of peaceful reflection and worship of the Holy Light. In the wake of King Thoras Trollbane's murder and the kingdom's subsequent collapse, the Sanctum has instead become a defensive retreat. Those seeking to breach the inner sanctum must contend not only with the royal guards garrisoned throughout the halls, but with the haunting reality of an ancient human lineage clinging to survival on its sacred threshold.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Sanctum?",a="The Sanctum is the inner area behind the Church of Light's chapel within Stromgarde Keep. It adjoins the keep's graveyard and leads directly into the ancestral Trollbane family crypt.",al={"what is sanctum","stromgarde sanctum","sanctum stromgarde keep"}},{q="Who controls the Sanctum right now?",a="The Sanctum is held by surviving Stromgarde soldiers loyal to the Alliance and Prince Galen Trollbane. Unlike the rest of the ruined city overrun by Syndicate bandits and Boulderfist ogres, the chapel and Sanctum remain under human guard.",al={"who is in the sanctum","sanctum guards","who holds the sanctum"}},{q="What lies beyond the Sanctum?",a="Past the Sanctum lies the Trollbane family crypt, where the fallen rulers of Stromgarde, including the recently slain King Thoras Trollbane, are entombed.",al={"where does sanctum lead","sanctum crypt","what is behind the sanctum"}},{q="Why is this area important to Stromgarde?",a="Beyond serving as a consecrated center of worship for the Holy Light, the Sanctum protects the royal resting place of Stromgarde's kings. For the surviving defenders, surrendering it would mean allowing invaders to desecrate their ancestors' graves.",al={"why care about sanctum","sanctum significance","why is sanctum defended"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The chapel and Sanctum represent the last unconsecrated sanctuaries of the Holy Light within the fallen capital of Arathi, making its defense a matter of solemn duty.",["faction:Alliance"]="Holding the Sanctum ensures the royal line of Trollbane retains a grasp on their ancestral seat, keeping the Alliance presence alive in the contested ruins of Stromgarde."},kw={"arathi","chapel","church of light","crypt","galen","sanctum","stromgarde","trollbane"},rel={"subzone:stromgarde-keep","subzone:crypt-stromgarde-keep","zone:arathi","topic:light","topic:alliance"},src={"Sanctum (Stromgarde Keep)"}}
E["subzone:stromgarde-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Stromgarde Keep",z="arathi",s="Stromgarde Keep is the battered, divided capital of the fallen human kingdom of Stromgarde in the Arathi Highlands. Once the proud cradle of human civilization known as Strom, the fortress is now partitioned between hostile Syndicate rogues, invading Boulderfist ogres, and a desperate remnant of royal defenders under Prince Galen Trollbane.",h="Stromgarde Keep is the battered, divided capital of the fallen human kingdom of Stromgarde in the Arathi...",sec={{t="Cradle of Humanity",b="Long before it bore its current name, this fortress was founded nearly three millennia ago as Strom, the first capital of the unified human empire of Arathor under King Thoradin. It served as the staging ground for humanity's victory against the forest trolls and was the birthplace of human wizardry, where high elven magi tutored the first hundred human spellcasters. Over centuries, as younger sister kingdoms like Dalaran, Lordaeron, and Stormwind rose and prospered, Strom's influence waned. Renamed Stromgarde by the stubborn Trollbane dynasty who stayed behind, it remained a proud warrior bastion throughout the Second War, anchoring the Alliance of Lordaeron against the Orcish Horde.",sp=0},{t="A Shattered Bastion",b="Following the devastation of the Third War, Stromgarde finally buckled under mounting catastrophes and treachery. Today, the majestic stone city sits fractured into three warring sectors. The aristocratic traitors of the Syndicate occupy the grand inner keep, while brutish Boulderfist ogres have overrun the former sanctum of the mage district. Pinned in the remaining quarter, Prince Galen Trollbane and the battered Stromgarde military wage a grueling, bloody war on multiple fronts just to keep their ancestral home from vanishing into memory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who controls Stromgarde Keep right now?",a="The ruined city is carved into three fiercely contested zones. The treacherous Syndicate controls the central inner keep, invading Boulderfist clan ogres occupy the ruined mage district, and Prince Galen Trollbane leads the surviving remnants of the Stromgarde army from the remaining quarter.",al={"who lives in stromgarde","who owns stromgarde keep","who is in stromgarde"}},{q="What was the Empire of Arathor?",a="The Empire of Arathor was the very first unified human nation, founded nearly three thousand years ago by King Thoradin. Its capital was Strom, situated on the very grounds where Stromgarde Keep stands today.",al={"what is strom","first human kingdom","arathor empire"}},{q="Why is the city in ruins?",a="Stromgarde stood as a powerhouse through the Second War, but the kingdom was left vulnerable and isolated in the chaotic aftermath of the Third War. A combination of internal betrayal, opportunistic attacks by the criminal Syndicate, and assaults from Boulderfist ogres shattered the city's defenses.",al={"why is stromgarde destroyed","what happened to stromgarde"}},{q="Who is Galen Trollbane?",a="Prince Galen Trollbane is the royal scion and commander of Stromgarde's surviving forces. From his embattled redoubt inside the keep, he directs the desperate defense against both the Syndicate and the ogres.",al={"prince trollbane","who is prince galen"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="Stromgarde was the ancient heart of your entire race, where the first human tribes banded together under Thoradin and learned the arcane arts from the high elves. Seeing it overrun by criminals and ogres is a bitter sight.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stromgarde was a founding member of the Alliance of Lordaeron during the Second War. Its beleaguered defenders represent one of the last loyal strongholds left in the north, fighting desperately to avoid total annihilation."},kw={"arathi","arathor","boulderfist","galen","strom","stromgarde","stromgarde keep","syndicate","thoradin","trollbane"},rel={"zone:arathi","topic:syndicate","topic:alliance-of-lordaeron","topic:second-war","topic:third-war","topic:stormwind-kingdom","topic:lordaeron","subzone:dalaran"},src={"Stromgarde Keep"}}
E["subzone:thandol-span"] = {t="subzone",n="Thandol Span",z="arathi",s="The Thandol Span is a pair of colossal dwarven stone bridges connecting the Wetlands of Khaz Modan with the Arathi Highlands of southern Lordaeron. Long celebrated as a marvel of engineering and the vital artery between the northern and southern kingdoms, it is currently in a state of disaster following a sabotage attack by Dark Iron infiltrators.",h="The Thandol Span is a pair of colossal dwarven stone bridges connecting the Wetlands of Khaz Modan with the...",sec={{t="A Lifeline Severed",b="Constructed following the War of the Three Hammers to bridge Ironforge with the Wildhammer clan of the Aerie Peak, the Thandol Span stands among the grandest stonecraft feats of dwarven history. Capable of supporting entire marching armies, it served as the critical land corridor between Lordaeron and Khaz Modan throughout the Second War, notably carrying Sir Anduin Lothar's counter-offensive southward. Today, the crossing is grievously wounded. Dark Iron saboteurs led by Balgaras the Foul and Kam Deepfury mounted a devastating assault from nearby Dun Modr, shattering one span entirely with explosives and threatening to sever overland travel between the allied realms completely.",sp=0},{t="The Fight for the Crossing",b="The surviving bridge remains contested and heavily guarded. Mountaineers from Ironforge fight desperately to preserve the remaining roadway and repel Dark Iron sappers, suffering painful losses in the process. The loss of the bridge would leave northern trade and military movements almost entirely reliant on maritime routes, cutting off Alliance forces stationed across the Arathi Highlands from immediate reinforcement.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Thandol Span?",a="It is a massive dwarven double-arched stone bridge spanning the deep canyon between the Wetlands in northern Khaz Modan and the Arathi Highlands in southern Lordaeron.",al={"thandol span overview","what is this bridge","thandol bridge"},it="place"},{q="Why is one of the bridges broken?",a="Dark Iron dwarves launched an assault from the captured outpost of Dun Modr, using high explosives to demolish one of the two spans in an attempt to cut Alliance supply lines.",al={"who blew up the bridge","thandol span destroyed","why is thandol span broken"},it="ruin"},{q="Why was the Thandol Span originally built?",a="Ironforge dwarves built the span after the War of the Three Hammers to foster trade, diplomacy, and enduring ties with their Wildhammer cousins living across the canyon in the north.",al={"who built thandol span","thandol history","why was it built"},it="origin"},{q="Did armies cross here during the Second War?",a="Yes. Although the Old Horde bypassed the bridges by crossing the sea to invade Lordaeron, Sir Anduin Lothar later led the Alliance counter-offensive across the Span to drive the orcs back into Khaz Modan.",al={"thandol span second war","orcs at thandol span","lothar thandol span"},it="history"},{q="Who controls the Thandol Span?",a="The Thandol Span is held and guarded by the dwarves of Ironforge, whose lineage—specifically the Anvilmar family—has overseen and protected the massive crossing for generations. Despite suffering brutal raids and sabotage from Dark Iron infiltrators operating out of nearby Dun Modr, Ironforge mountaineers continue to defend the surviving bridge, keeping open the vital link between Khaz Modan and the northern kingdoms.",al={"who controls thandol span","who runs thandol span","thandol span guards"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is the Thandol Span dangerous?",a="Yes, traveling across the Span is hazardous. Dark Iron saboteurs recently infiltrated the gorge and detonated explosives, completely severing one of the two twin arches and leaving the remaining span vulnerable. Hostile Dark Iron dwarves linger nearby in the northern Wetlands and around Dun Modr, actively plotting further strikes against travelers and Ironforge defenders holding the line.",al={"is thandol span safe","thandol span danger","threats at thandol span"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="For the dwarves of Ironforge, the Span represents both a masterwork of their stonemasons and a painful battleground where Dark Iron kin have brought destruction to their front door.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Span is the sole direct overland link uniting Khaz Modan with the beleaguered northern outposts of Lordaeron, making its defense vital to the war effort."},kw={"arathi highlands","balgaras","dark iron","dun modr","ironforge","kam deepfury","thandol span","wetlands"},rel={"subzone:dun-modr","zone:wetlands","zone:arathi","quest:631","quest:303","quest:378","npc:kam-deepfury","topic:second-war"},src={"Thandol Span"}}
E["subzone:thoradin-s-wall"] = {t="subzone",n="Thoradin's Wall",z="arathi",s="Thoradin's Wall is a monumental, crumbling stone rampart dividing the Arathi Highlands from the Hillsbrad Foothills. Commissioned millennia ago by King Thoradin during the dawn of the Empire of Arathor, it was built to shield early humanity from the fierce incursions of the Amani trolls.",h="Thoradin's Wall is a monumental, crumbling stone rampart dividing the Arathi Highlands from the Hillsbrad...",sec={{t="A Bulwark of Ancient Arathor",b="Erected nearly three thousand years ago, Thoradin's Wall marks the western frontier of ancient Strom, the heart of the first unified human empire. King Thoradin recognized that humanity's fledgeling settlements were acutely vulnerable to the predatory raids of the Amani forest trolls. By raising this vast stone barrier across the valley corridor, Arathor secured its heartland and forged a defensible bastion from which humanity could survive and eventually contest troll supremacy in the north.",sp=0},{t="Centuries of Decay",b="Today, the ancient barrier stands in severe disrepair. Vast breeches gash the stone ramparts, their battlements weathered down by thousands of years of exposure, warfare, and abandonment. Following the splintering of Arathor into rival kingdoms and the eventual fall of neighboring Lordaeron to the Scourge, no central realm maintains the masonry. Now, travelers and roaming bandits slip freely through its broken archways as they journey between Hillsbrad and the untamed Arathi Highlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who built Thoradin's Wall?",a="It was commissioned by King Thoradin, the founder and warlord who unified humanity's tribes to establish the Empire of Arathor nearly three millennia ago.",al={"who made thoradins wall","creator of thoradins wall","thoradin wall origins"},it="origin"},{q="Why was the wall built in the first place?",a="King Thoradin ordered its construction to defend humanity's early capital, Strom, and its fledgling settlements from the fierce raids of the neighboring Amani troll empire.",al={"purpose of thoradins wall","why build the wall","what was thoradins wall for"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the wall so broken down today?",a="The wall has suffered thousands of years of natural weathering, conflict, and neglect. After the Empire of Arathor splintered into independent human nations, the grand frontier fortification lost its strategic priority and was left to decay.",al={"why is thoradin wall broken","who destroyed thoradins wall","why ruined"},it="ruin"},{q="What regions does Thoradin's Wall separate?",a="The wall forms the natural overland border separating the lush Hillsbrad Foothills to the west from the rugged Arathi Highlands to the east.",al={"where is thoradins wall","what does the wall divide","border of thoradins wall"}},{q="What is Thoradin's Wall?",a="Thoradin's Wall is an ancient, colossal stone rampart that spans the border between the Arathi Highlands and Hillsbrad Foothills. Raised millennia ago during the height of the Empire of Arathor, it served as humanity's grand defensive bulwark to shield the heartlands around Strom from the fierce incursions of the Amani trolls. Today, though heavily weathered and broken, its towering arches and crumbling stones still loom over the trade road.",al={"what is thoradins wall","thoradin wall info","about thoradins wall"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at Thoradin's Wall?",a="For generations, the wall held firm against countless raids by the forest trolls of Zul'Aman, defending humanity's cradle. Ancient tales also tell of a dark time during the empire when a terrifying curse mutated beasts and men alike, sending a horde of twisted monstrosities crashing into and breaching the wall. Over subsequent centuries, neglect, wars, and the sheer passage of time saw its defenses decay into the ruins standing today.",al={"history of thoradins wall","thoradins wall battles","what happened here"},it="history",add=true},{q="Why is it called Thoradin's Wall?",a="The wall is named in honor of High King Thoradin, the legendary warlord who first unified the warring human tribes into the glorious Empire of Arathor. Shortly after establishing his empire and founding its great capital of Strom, Thoradin ordered the construction of this vast fortification to secure mankind's survival against hostile wilderness threats, ensuring his name remained etched in stone across the frontier.",al={"why is it called thoradins wall","who is thoradins wall named after","thoradin wall name"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["race:Human"]="Standing before the wall is a solemn brush with human antiquity, showcasing the enduring masonry of King Thoradin, who first unified the scattered human tribes.",["race:Troll"]="The ruined fortifications are a stark reminder of the ancient territorial wars where humanity successfully halted the domain of the forest trolls."},kw={"amani","arathi","arathor","hillsbrad","strom","thoradin","thoradin's wall","wall"},rel={"zone:arathi","zone:hillsbrad","topic:troll","topic:dwarf","topic:syndicate"},src={"Thoradin's Wall"}}
E["subzone:tower-of-arathor"] = {t="subzone",n="Tower of Arathor",z="arathi",s="The Tower of Arathor is a ruined wizard's tower situated in the former mage district in the southwestern reaches of Stromgarde Keep. Once the workshop of Archmage Trelane, it was overrun during the fall of the city and is currently occupied by Boulderfist ogres.",h="The Tower of Arathor is a ruined wizard's tower situated in the former mage district in the southwestern...",sec={{t="A Bastion Overrun",b="Erected in the heart of Stromgarde Keep's mage district and named after the ancient Empire of Arathor, this spire long served the realm's sorcerers. Its most notable resident, Archmage Trelane, devised a magical defensive grid keyed to enchanted gemstones to protect the sanctum. However, when the Syndicate and the Boulderfist ogre clan assaulted Stromgarde following the Third War, the kingdom fractured. Despite Trelane's desperate attempts to hold the tower using his arcane wards, the sheer brutish force of the ogres overwhelmed him. Forced to flee the city for his life, the archmage left behind his most prized arcane artifacts, leaving the spire in the hands of the Boulderfist brute Ruul Onestone and his followers.",sp=0},{t="Reclaiming the Lost Relics",b="Even in exile, Trelane refused to abandon his life's work. Enlisting the aid of his former pupil, Archmage Malin of the Kirin Tor, an expedition was mounted to retrieve his phylactery, orb, and ember agate from the ruins. Operating out of Refuge Pointe, Malin's agents discovered that the ogres had pillaged the stones required to command the tower's automated defenses. By crafting a replacement enchanted agate and placing it upon the pedestals framing the tower's threshold, conjured water elementals could be awakened to purge the ogre occupiers and allow daring adventurers to recover the archmage's heirlooms.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Tower of Arathor?",a="It is a mage tower located in the southwestern ruins of Stromgarde Keep. Named in honor of the ancient human empire of Arathor, it served as a center of study for the kingdom's mages until it fell to invading ogres.",al={"tower of arathor","stromgarde mage tower","arathi tower"}},{q="Who lives in the tower now?",a="The tower and the surrounding mage district are occupied by Boulderfist ogres. Inside the spire dwells the ogre mage Ruul Onestone along with his guards, who have rooted out and guarded the relics left behind by its former master.",al={"who is in the tower of arathor","tower of arathor mobs","tower of arathor boss"}},{q="Who was Archmage Trelane?",a="Archmage Trelane was a prominent wizard of Stromgarde who lived and studied in the tower. He created its gemstone-powered warding systems and fled into exile after failing to defend the sanctum against the Boulderfist assault.",al={"archmage trelane","who owned the tower","trelane"}},{q="How do the tower's defenses work?",a="Trelane keyed the tower to activate when an enchanted agate is placed against the pedestals flanking its entrance. When activated, the arcane matrix conjures hostile water elementals that battle any intruders occupying the entrance.",al={"how to activate tower defenses","trelane's defenses","tower pedestals"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The tower serves as a sobering reminder of what happened to Stromgarde's arcane enclave, while showcasing Archmage Trelane's clever mastery over defensive elemental constructs.",["faction:Alliance"]="Stromgarde Keep is contested ground; helping Archmage Malin's agents recover Trelane's lost artifacts denies potent magical relics to the encroaching Boulderfist clan."},kw={"arathi","boulderfist","malin","ruul onestone","skuerto","stromgarde","tower of arathor","trelane"},rel={"subzone:stromgarde-keep","zone:arathi","npc:archmage-malin","npc:skuerto","quest:690","topic:syndicate","topic:alliance","topic:third-war"},src={"Tower of Arathor"}}
E["subzone:witherbark-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Witherbark Village",z="arathi",s="Witherbark Village is a forest troll settlement nestled around a secluded lake in the southeastern hills of the Arathi Highlands. Inhabited by the hostile Witherbark tribe, it serves as a staging ground for troll raiders contesting both the Alliance remnants of Stromgarde and the Horde outpost at Hammerfall.",h="Witherbark Village is a forest troll settlement nestled around a secluded lake in the southeastern hills of...",sec={{t="Stronghold of the Forest Trolls",b="Built along the shores of a quiet mountain lake, Witherbark Village houses the fierce forest trolls of the Witherbark tribe. While fishers, axe throwers, and witch doctors occupy the hut-lined waterfront, tribal leaders such as Zalas Witherbark and deadly shadow hunters oversee operations from a massive cavern cavern tucked behind the settlement. The Witherbark maintain an opportunistic alliance with the Boulderfist ogres of Arathi, working together to carve out territory across the highlands—even establishing a firm foothold amidst the ruins of Stromgarde Keep. Fiercely territorial, they lash out at any outsider venturing into their corner of the basin.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in Witherbark Village?",a="The settlement is held by the Witherbark tribe, a faction of forest trolls indigenous to the region. They field headhunters, axe throwers, fishers, and witch doctors who defend the lake and surrounding paths.",al={"who are witherbark","witherbark trolls","who controls witherbark village"}},{q="What is inside the large cave behind the village?",a="The cavern serves as the seat of tribal leadership. Chieftain Zalas Witherbark and dangerous shadow hunters coordinate the tribe's raids and defenses from deep within its tunnels.",al={"witherbark cave","cave behind witherbark village","zalas witherbark location"}},{q="Why are the Witherbark trolls working with ogres?",a="The Witherbark have struck a loose alliance of convenience with the local Boulderfist ogres. Combining their strength allows them to press against the weakened human defenders of Stromgarde and threaten regional rivals like the Horde in Hammerfall.",al={"witherbark ogre alliance","trolls and boulderfist","why are trolls allied with ogres"}},{q="Are the Witherbark friendly to the Horde?",a="No. Like most Amani-descended forest trolls, the Witherbark harbor bitter resentment toward the modern Horde and its Darkspear trolls, and they fight the Horde at Hammerfall. They will attack Horde travelers on sight.",al={"are witherbark horde","can horde talk to witherbark","witherbark reputation"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Witherbark show no deference to the new Horde, frequently clashing with scouts from Hammerfall and threatening travel through the eastern passes.",["race:Troll"]="Darkspear trolls will find no kinship here; the forest trolls of the Witherbark view jungle trolls and the Horde with deep-seated hostility."},kw={"arathi highlands","forest trolls","nimar the slayer","witherbark","witherbark village","zalas witherbark"},rel={"zone:arathi","subzone:hammerfall","topic:troll","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Witherbark Village"}}
E["zone:arathi"] = {t="zone",n="Arathi Highlands",z="arathi",s="The Arathi Highlands are a rugged plateau in southeastern Lordaeron, renowned as the ancient birthplace of the Empire of Arathor. Today, the kingdom of Stromgarde lies in ruins, leaving the craggy realm engulfed in multi-front warfare between the remnants of Stromgarde, the Horde, criminal Syndicate nobles, and invading ogres.",h="The Arathi Highlands are a rugged plateau in southeastern Lordaeron, renowned as the ancient birthplace of...",sec={{t="Cradle of Humanity",b="Millennia ago, King Thoradin united the fractured human tribes under the banner of the Arathi, constructing the majestic capital of Strom across these dry, defensible plains. It was here that humanity forged its legendary compact with the high elves during the Troll Wars, mastering the arcane arts to push back the Amani. Over time, noble bloodlines migrated north into Lordaeron and south toward Stormwind, but the imperial guard stayed behind to form the martial realm of Stromgarde. For ages, Stromgarde stood as a bastion of stalwart warriors dedicated to keeping the forest trolls at bay.",sp=0},{t="A Shattered Kingdom",b="Stromgarde proved vital in defending the Alliance during the Second War under King Thoras Trollbane, but the Third War and its aftermath shattered the nation. Although the kingdom spared itself the worst ravages of the Scourge plague, the mysterious death of King Thoras threw the realm into turmoil. Boulderfist ogres swept in from the hills, while the traitorous Alteraci nobles of the Syndicate seized sprawling districts of Stromgarde Keep. Today, Prince Galen Trollbane and his loyalist survivors cling to a tiny sliver of the city and their redoubt at Refuge Pointe, waging a bitter guerrilla war against hopeless odds.",sp=0},{t="The War for the Highlands",b="Arathi is a fiercely contested crossroads. In the northeast, the Horde converted an abandoned human internment camp into Hammerfall, named in honor of the legendary Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer, using it as an anchor to secure their northern holdings and safeguard allies in Hillsbrad. Meanwhile, the Witherbark troll tribe seeks vengeance against their ancient human persecutors, and the Argus Wake pulls strings behind the Syndicate's occupation. At the center of the plateau lie ancient Circles of Binding, where bound elementals restrain an enigmatic, ancient power buried beneath the stone.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to Stromgarde Keep?",a="Following King Thoras Trollbane's death, Stromgarde succumbed to internal strife and overwhelming assaults. Boulderfist ogres seized the city's exterior districts while the opportunistic Syndicate seized the sanctum, leaving Prince Galen Trollbane and his dwindling garrison clinging to a single fortified corner while fighting desperate battles inside their own capital.",al={"why is stromgarde ruined","who controls stromgarde","stromgarde status"}},{q="What is Hammerfall?",a="Hammerfall is a fortified Horde outpost built within the remnants of a human internment camp where orcs were held after the Second War. It was named to honor former Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer, who fell leading the campaign to liberate the captives held across Lordaeron's camps.",al={"horde base arathi","history of hammerfall","why is it called hammerfall"}},{q="Where does the Alliance operate in Arathi?",a="Alliance soldiers and Stromgarde defenders stage their operations out of Refuge Pointe, a naturally fortified canyon in the center of the highlands. From here, they launch sorties to reclaim Stromgarde Keep and fight back encroaching ogres and trolls.",al={"alliance base arathi","refuge pointe","where are the stromgarde humans"}},{q="What are the stone circles across the plains?",a="The Circles of Binding—Inner, Outer, East, and West—are ancient magical seals maintained and guarded by rogue elementals. They serve to imprison an unknown, primordial entity buried deep beneath the highlands.",al={"circles of binding","elementals in arathi","stone circles"}},{q="How do you reach the Arathi Highlands?",a="Travelers from the north and west pass through the breach in Thoradin's Wall from the Hillsbrad Foothills. Travelers arriving from Khaz Modan in the south cross the massive dwarven bridge of the Thandol Span, which spans the chasm separating the highlands from the Wetlands.",al={"getting to arathi","how to get to arathi highlands","arathi entrance"}},{q="What is the Syndicate doing in Arathi?",a="The Syndicate consists of exiled Alteraci nobility seeking to carve out new domains by pillaging fallen realms. In Arathi, they have overrun large sections of Stromgarde Keep and outlying farms like Northfold Manor, secretly guided by the dark cultists of the Argus Wake.",al={"why is syndicate in arathi","syndicate stromgarde","who leads the syndicate here"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Human"]="Every human kingdom traces its roots to the Empire of Arathor; seeing the seat of human civilization broken and overrun by ogres and thieves is a profound cultural tragedy.",["faction:Horde"]="Hammerfall stands as sacred ground to the modern Horde—a monument to Orgrim Doomhammer's sacrifice that freed an enslaved people from internment.",["class:Warrior"]="Stromgarde produced the most celebrated frontline martial tradition on Azeroth, making its rugged battlegrounds a revered trial by arms.",["profession:Mining"]="The craggy ridges of Arathi are rich in iron and mithril, and Drywhisker Gorge is the only known source of lesser bloodstone ore."},kw={"arathi","arathi highlands","arathor","boulderfist","galen trollbane","hammerfall","refuge pointe","stromgarde","syndicate","thandol span","thoradin's wall"},rel={"subzone:stromgarde-keep","subzone:hammerfall","subzone:refuge-pointe","subzone:thandol-span","subzone:thoradin-s-wall","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","zone:hillsbrad","zone:wetlands"},src={"Arathi Highlands (Classic)","Arathi Highlands"}}
